": "english", "review": "No controller support? This isn't deluxe at all.", "timestamp_created": 1783236408, "timestamp_updated": 1783236408, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 6, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.533052563667297363", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "229652971", "author": {"steamid": "76561197976585197", "personaname": "RRCM (Rico)", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/rrcmrico/", "num_games_owned": 9813, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 3308, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3308, "last_played": 1783239660, "avatar": "017c03ab5dab92cd725d2d21afe3e9f9544d382e"}, "language": "english", "review": "\"We're sorry, an error has occurred\"\n\nAs of 7/4/2026 there seem to be EA server issue(s) that prevents launching this game with a product key activation error. This workaround helped me to get the game running again:\n\nhttps://www.reddit.com/r/MECoOp/comments/189u76r/mass_effect_3_product_key_could_not_activate/\n\nNever buy this game for anything more than a deep discount as you may lose access to it over time. If you can get the game to work, then it is worth playing for an overall compelling singleplayer story campaign (which pays off more if you played the two prior games), interesting world building, well written character interactions, fun though albeit clunky combat gameplay, and decent co-op horde mode multiplayer.", "timestamp_created": 1783231038, "timestamp_updated": 1783240225, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.550802111625671387", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "hardware": 